# Documentation First

## Objective

Meaningful changes (features, fixes, architecture, performance) should be **taught in documentation**  -  not only implemented in code.

## Documentation Folder

**This repo:** use `doku/` (see `doku-pflicht.mdc`) — especially `doku/aenderungen/` for every code change, plus `doku/module/` and architecture notes as needed. Do not use `/docs` here; that path is for other projects that still use it.

## What to Document

- What changed and why.
- How to use or operate new behavior.
- Trade-offs and alternatives considered.
- Bug root causes and prevention when valuable (`knowledge-preservation.mdc`).

## Style

Clear, practical, example-driven. Assume a motivated developer new to this area of the codebase.

## Cross-links

`explain-decisions.mdc`, `knowledge-preservation.mdc`.

## Golden Rule

The project should get smarter every time you ship  -  not only larger.